WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:12.080
Not even close.

2
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:26.160
Take Oriva,

3
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.180
the coffee roaster.

4
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.140
Its promise,

5
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:29.840
roasted the week you order,

6
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.500
is on the bag already.

7
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:32.740
On the back,

8
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.100
in tiny grey type.

9
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.680
So buyers grab

10
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:36.800
the cheaper one.

11
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:37.660
And the founders

12
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:38.920
want a new logo.

13
00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:39.880
One each.

14
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.340
Hold that thought.

15
00:00:41.651 --> 00:00:43.351
So nobody draws yet.

16
00:00:43.391 --> 00:00:44.911
First, the direction:

17
00:00:45.291 --> 00:00:46.711
the look and feel.

18
00:00:47.082 --> 00:00:48.182
Three directions,

19
00:00:48.442 --> 00:00:49.602
each with a mood board

20
00:00:49.642 --> 00:00:51.262
and a style scape.

21
00:00:51.562 --> 00:00:53.202
Then the test most people skip:

22
00:00:53.462 --> 00:00:54.042
the shelf,

23
00:00:54.082 --> 00:00:55.622
beside the rivals.

24
00:00:56.182 --> 00:00:56.822
A and B?

25
00:00:56.862 --> 00:00:57.182
Lovely.

26
00:00:57.222 --> 00:00:58.402
And gone.

27
00:00:58.982 --> 00:00:59.842
C, night

28
00:00:59.882 --> 00:01:00.802
blue and pink,

29
00:01:00.842 --> 00:01:01.902
is the only

30
00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:03.022
bag you see.

31
00:01:03.302 --> 00:01:04.542
The shelf picked it,

32
00:01:04.582 --> 00:01:05.342
not taste.

33
00:01:05.748 --> 00:01:06.568
But a direction

34
00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:07.828
isn’t a logo.

35
00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:09.268
So now we draw.

36
00:01:09.648 --> 00:01:10.168
A lot.

37
00:01:10.471 --> 00:01:12.091
Over two hundred sketches,

38
00:01:12.451 --> 00:01:14.211
the founders’ favourites included.

39
00:01:14.571 --> 00:01:15.771
Each round asks:

40
00:01:16.211 --> 00:01:17.211
does it say fresh?

41
00:01:17.611 --> 00:01:18.851
The pile shrinks.

42
00:01:19.211 --> 00:01:20.691
Neither favourite makes it.

43
00:01:20.731 --> 00:01:21.251
Sorry.

44
00:01:25.891 --> 00:01:26.431
Polished.

45
00:01:27.031 --> 00:01:27.971
Now it has to survive

46
00:01:28.011 --> 00:01:28.911
other people.

47
00:01:29.397 --> 00:01:30.357
That’s what a design

48
00:01:30.397 --> 00:01:31.777
system is for:

49
00:01:32.537 --> 00:01:33.277
rules that stop

50
00:01:33.317 --> 00:01:34.717
a logo drifting.

51
00:01:35.117 --> 00:01:35.577
Watch.

52
00:01:36.075 --> 00:01:37.595
The printer stretches it.

53
00:01:37.635 --> 00:01:38.515
A café menu

54
00:01:38.555 --> 00:01:39.675
turns it purple.

55
00:01:40.055 --> 00:01:40.655
So the colours

56
00:01:40.695 --> 00:01:42.215
get exact values,

57
00:01:42.255 --> 00:01:43.615
the logo a grid,

58
00:01:43.835 --> 00:01:45.575
the type its sizes.

59
00:01:45.935 --> 00:01:46.695
And a bean pattern

60
00:01:46.735 --> 00:01:48.055
says Oriva,

61
00:01:48.095 --> 00:01:49.395
even with no logo.

62
00:01:49.855 --> 00:01:50.375
Boring?

63
00:01:50.415 --> 00:01:50.955
Very.

64
00:01:51.295 --> 00:01:52.535
That’s why it all matches.

65
00:01:52.924 --> 00:01:54.564
So everything people hold

66
00:01:54.604 --> 00:01:55.764
gets rebuilt.

67
00:01:56.144 --> 00:01:56.964
The card.

68
00:01:57.304 --> 00:01:58.184
The letterhead.

69
00:01:58.384 --> 00:01:59.044
The slides.

70
00:01:59.444 --> 00:02:00.344
The uniform.

71
00:02:00.744 --> 00:02:02.064
The flag outside.

72
00:02:02.524 --> 00:02:03.824
And that roast date,

73
00:02:03.864 --> 00:02:05.264
tiny, on the back?

74
00:02:05.304 --> 00:02:06.444
It moves to the front,

75
00:02:06.484 --> 00:02:07.584
big and pink.

76
00:02:07.844 --> 00:02:08.744
Now the bag says it

77
00:02:08.784 --> 00:02:09.984
from across the aisle:

78
00:02:10.184 --> 00:02:11.564
roasted this week.

79
00:02:11.841 --> 00:02:13.561
But we don’t stay forever.

80
00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:14.701
So Brand Automation

81
00:02:14.741 --> 00:02:15.961
keeps the team on brand,

82
00:02:16.001 --> 00:02:17.381
without a designer

83
00:02:17.421 --> 00:02:18.541
for every post.

84
00:02:18.886 --> 00:02:20.186
Posts become templates,

85
00:02:20.226 --> 00:02:21.226
with the brand

86
00:02:21.266 --> 00:02:22.326
locked in.

87
00:02:22.666 --> 00:02:23.506
One master file

88
00:02:23.546 --> 00:02:25.606
resizes to every format.

89
00:02:25.946 --> 00:02:27.086
Then someone makes a post

90
00:02:27.126 --> 00:02:28.226
in the old brown.

91
00:02:28.686 --> 00:02:29.426
It happens.

92
00:02:29.866 --> 00:02:30.886
The checker flags it

93
00:02:30.926 --> 00:02:32.246
before it goes out.

94
00:02:32.666 --> 00:02:33.086
Caught,

95
00:02:33.426 --> 00:02:33.906
fixed,

96
00:02:34.366 --> 00:02:34.846
posted.

97
00:02:35.322 --> 00:02:37.002
Here’s what Oriva has now.

98
00:02:37.363 --> 00:02:39.203
So, was it a new logo?

99
00:02:39.623 --> 00:02:40.743
A small part.

100
00:02:41.063 --> 00:02:41.943
One bean,

101
00:02:41.983 --> 00:02:42.783
one line.

102
00:02:43.103 --> 00:02:44.563
The rest is the system

103
00:02:44.603 --> 00:02:45.663
around it.

104
00:02:45.703 --> 00:02:46.983
Don’t ask what you like.

105
00:02:47.323 --> 00:02:48.603
Ask what your buyers

106
00:02:48.643 --> 00:02:49.583
will notice.

107
00:02:49.883 --> 00:02:50.743
On the shelf,

108
00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:52.163
people spot Oriva

109
00:02:52.203 --> 00:02:53.903
before they read a word.

110
00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.680
But a checker only works

111
00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:57.420
if someone knows why.

112
00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.040
And the why lives

113
00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.860
in two people’s heads.

114
00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:01.940
So what happens

115
00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:02.920
when they’re busy?

116
00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:06.000
That’s the Playbook.

